Source: move-bringup
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Move Port <move-port@localhost>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               dh-dkms,
               dh-sequence-dkms
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/local/move-bringup
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: ablspi-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, dkms
Description: ablspi kernel module for the Ableton Move (DKMS source)
 Clean-room re-implementation of the ablspi SPI character driver that
 carries audio, MIDI, and display data between the Move's Linux SoC
 (CM4 or CM5) and its XMOS I/O microcontroller.
 .
 Exposes /dev/ablspi%d.%d with a 4 KB mmap-able shared buffer and the
 13-entry ioctl ABI defined by Ableton's GPL move-spi user-space library.
 Builds for any kernel >= 6.6 via DKMS.

Package: move-bringup
Architecture: arm64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends},
         ablspi-dkms,
         adduser,
         avahi-daemon,
         dbus,
         device-tree-compiler,
         libnss-mdns,
         python3,
         python3-dbus-next,
         systemd-sysv,
         udev
Recommends: u-boot-tools, util-linux (>= 2.35), parted, e2fsprogs,
            network-manager, iw, coreutils (>= 8.30)
Description: Ableton Move userspace bring-up files
 Installs everything needed to run the stock Ableton Move user space
 (/opt/move) on a Debian arm64 image: the ableton user and ablspi group,
 udev rule for /dev/ablspi*, DBus system policy and service files,
 modules-load.d entry, and systemd units for MoveLauncher, the web
 service, the NCM USB-Ethernet gadget, and the XMOS power sequencer.
 .
 Pulls in avahi-daemon and libnss-mdns so the device is reachable as
 move.local over mDNS/Bonjour and so MoveLauncher's org.freedesktop.Avahi
 D-Bus query for the hostname succeeds.
 .
 Does NOT include the Ableton-proprietary /opt/move binaries themselves;
 you must populate /opt/move from your existing Move image (or from
 Ableton's official update payload) before enabling the services.
